  "body": "Scale-dependent seed switching was proposed as a way to improve recursive cost using a log-scale average of seed exponents. This package gives an exact counterexample to that unconditional substitution in the stated positive recurrence: two complete profiles with roots 1/4 and 3/4 yield p_eff=log_256(19+3 sqrt(33)) in (5/8,2/3), rather than 1/2. The predecessor's explicit oscillation-error bound permits the discrepancy; a sublinear error estimate is needed before dropping it.\n\nA separate positive-tree comparison proves that arbitrary per-node switching cannot beat the best fixed seed in a finite positive catalogue with zero glue, bounded child ratios and unit terminal cost. That limited extremal conclusion survives independently of root averaging. Both child ranks, all multiplicities and terminal overshoot are retained; a unit additive toll leaves the counterexample exponent unchanged. No physical seed, supplier admission, outer transfer or new kappa is claimed.\n\nValidation: registered CPython 3.12.12 replay with `-I -O -B`; a separate mathematical worker's exact rank-history implementation (1,023 schedules and 112,311 total rank histories); 11 semantic controls across the two implementations; exact committed-byte preflight; Git-free read-only CPython 3.14.6 replay. These support written all-scale proofs, not formal-kernel or independent human review. No selected cold replay was needed or performed; selected binding check passes.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/scale-dependent-seed-moment-audit\n```\n\nScientific base c7df0bb890cae0cc393cdd32dad19c3facc80992 is retained. Canonical main refreshed to a7fc79c0cd63d6aa48df753069fc49eabda79dc3 at 06:48:47 UTC, priority revision 5; relevant guidance and selected record unchanged, and the package patch applies cleanly. Inspected predecessor: Philippe Van Velzen/philippeVV single-letter lane at ed21d6245f8ce1a62e21205be7bedc24271dd772; full source/blob/hash pins and attribution are in SOURCES.json. No predecessor implementation is imported. Live overlap before submission covered 491 open PRs incl drafts, 2,088 closed/merged PRs and 1,526 Discussion records with complete pagination, plus local notes; metadata snapshots exclude arbitrary diffs and are not a novelty guarantee.\n\nCanonical finding/claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2278#discussioncomment-18965872. Prepared by Ross Richardson with substantial OpenAI Codex GPT-6.1 Sol Max assistance and one independent AI mathematical worker. Apache-2.0.\n\n\n**Review follow-up:** current head `36622e0bd376cf56a0acf54045469bac094d0d94` corrects only the coverage field names in `REVIEW.md`: `homogeneous_cases=240`, `homogeneous_max_index=120`. Complete registered replay and eight-file committed-byte validation pass at this head; separate proof/source audit found no substantive defect. Scientific/code/metadata files and result remain unchanged. Current CI is separate in the follow-up comment.",
